{"id":"mahabharata-3-113","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":113,"title":"त्रयोदशाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 113 · Rishyashringa brings rain to Anga","summary":{"en":"Vibhandaka warns that such beings are demons, but when he is away again the courtesan returns and takes Rishyashringa on her boat to Anga. Rain falls as he arrives, Lomapada gives him his daughter Shanta, and Vibhandaka, appeased by the honours paid him, accepts the marriage.","kn":"ಅಂಥವರು ರಾಕ್ಷಸರು ಎಂದು ವಿಭಾಂಡಕರು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಆದರೆ ಅವರು ಮತ್ತೆ ಹೊರಗಿದ್ದಾಗ ವೇಶ್ಯೆ ಬಂದು ಋಶ್ಯಶೃಂಗನನ್ನು ದೋಣಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಅಂಗದೇಶಕ್ಕೆ ಒಯ್ಯುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಅವನು ಬರುತ್ತಲೇ ಮಳೆ ಬೀಳುತ್ತದೆ, ಲೋಮಪಾದನು ಮಗಳು ಶಾಂತೆಯನ್ನು ಕೊಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಸಲ್ಲಿಸಿದ ಗೌರವದಿಂದ ಶಾಂತರಾದ ವಿಭಾಂಡಕರು ವಿವಾಹವನ್ನು ಒಪ್ಪುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"विभाण्डक चेतावनी देते हैं कि ऐसे प्राणी राक्षस होते हैं, पर उनके फिर बाहर जाने पर वेश्या लौटकर ऋष्यशृङ्ग को नाव से अङ्ग ले जाती है। उनके पहुँचते ही वर्षा होती है, लोमपाद अपनी पुत्री शान्ता उन्हें देते हैं, और सम्मान से प्रसन्न विभाण्डक विवाह स्वीकार करते हैं।","te":"అలాంటివారు రాక్షసులని విభాండకుడు హెచ్చరిస్తాడు, కానీ ఆయన మళ్లీ బయటకు వెళ్లినప్పుడు వేశ్య వచ్చి ఋశ్యశృంగుని పడవలో అంగదేశానికి తీసుకువెళ్తుంది. అతడు రాగానే వర్షం కురుస్తుంది, లోమపాదుడు కుమార్తె శాంతను ఇస్తాడు; చేసిన సత్కారాలకు శాంతించిన విభాండకుడు వివాహాన్ని అంగీకరిస్తాడు.","ta":"அத்தகையோர் அரக்கர்கள் என்று விபாண்டகர் எச்சரிக்க, அவர் மீண்டும் வெளியே சென்றபோது கணிகை வந்து ருஶ்யஶ்ருங்கரைப் படகில் அங்க நாட்டுக்கு அழைத்துச் செல்கிறாள். அவர் வந்ததும் மழை பெய்ய, லோமபாதன் தன் மகள் ஶாந்தையை அவருக்கு மணமுடிக்கிறான்; அளிக்கப்பட்ட மரியாதையால் அமைதியடைந்த விபாண்டகர் மணத்தை ஏற்கிறார்.","ml":"ഇത്തരക്കാർ രാക്ഷസന്മാരാണെന്ന് വിഭാണ്ഡകൻ മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു; പക്ഷേ അദ്ദേഹം വീണ്ടും പോയപ്പോൾ ഗണിക മടങ്ങിയെത്തി ഋഷ്യശൃംഗനെ തോണിയിൽ അംഗരാജ്യത്തേക്ക് കൊണ്ടുപോകുന്നു. അവിടെ എത്തിയപ്പോൾ മഴ പെയ്യുന്നു; ലോമപാദൻ തന്റെ മകൾ ശാന്തയെ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് നൽകുന്നു; ലഭിച്ച ആദരവിൽ സന്തുഷ്ടനായ വിഭാണ്ഡകൻ വിവാഹത്തിന് സമ്മതിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.113; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"विभाण्डक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vibhandaka said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"रक्षांसि चैतानि चरन्ति पुत्र\nरूपेण तेनाद्भुतदर्शनेन ।\nअतुल्यरूपाण्यतिघोरवन्ति\nविघ्नं सदा तपसश्चिन्तयन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son, these are rakshasas who roam in that wonderful form. Incomparable and very terrible, they are always thinking how to obstruct austerity."}},{"n":2,"text":"सुरूपरूपाणि च तानि तात\nप्रलोभयन्ते विविधैरुपायैः ।\nसुखाच्च लोकाच्च निपातयन्ति\nतान्युग्रकर्माणि मुनीन्वनेषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Handsome in form, dear son, they tempt in many ways and cast down sages in the forests from happiness and from the worlds, those cruel ones."}},{"n":3,"text":"न तानि सेवेत मुनिर्यतात्मा\nसतां लोकान्प्रार्थयानः कथंचित् ।\nकृत्वा विघ्नं तापसानां रमन्ते\nपापाचारास्तपसस्तान्यपाप ॥","meaning":{"en":"A self-controlled sage seeking the worlds of the good should never go near them. Those evildoers delight in blocking ascetics, sinless one."}},{"n":4,"text":"असज्जनेनाचरितानि पुत्र\nपापान्यपेयानि मधूनि तानि ।\nमाल्यानि चैतानि न वै मुनीनां\nस्मृतानि चित्रोज्ज्वलगन्धवन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son, those sweet drinks are sins done by the wicked and not to be drunk, and these garlands, brightly coloured and scented, are not remembered as sages' things."}},{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"रक्षांसि तानीति निवार्य पुत्रं\nविभाण्डकस्तां मृगयां बभूव ।\nनासादयामास यदा त्र्यहेण\nतदा स पर्याववृतेऽऽश्रमाय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Telling his son they were rakshasas, Vibhandaka went out to find her. When after three days he did not find her, he returned to his hermitage."}},{"n":6,"text":"यदा पुनः काश्यपो वै जगाम\nफलान्याहर्तुं विधिना श्रामणेन ।\nतदा पुनर्लोभयितुं जगाम\nसा वेशयोषा मुनिमृश्यशृङ्गम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Kashyapa went again to fetch fruit by the rule of ascetics, the courtesan went again to tempt the sage Rishyashringa."}},{"n":7,"text":"दृष्ट्वैव तामृश्यशृङ्गः प्रहृष्टः\nसंभ्रान्तरूपोऽभ्यपतत्तदानीम् ।\nप्रोवाच चैनां भवतोऽऽश्रमाय\nगच्छाव यावन्न पिता ममैति ॥","meaning":{"en":"On seeing her, Rishyashringa, delighted and flustered, rushed forward and said to her, \"Let us go to your hermitage before my father returns.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"ततो राजन्काश्यपस्यैकपुत्रं\nप्रवेश्य योगेन विमुच्य नावम् ।\nप्रलोभयन्त्यो विविधैरुपायै-\nराजग्मुरङ्गाधिपतेः समीपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, by a stratagem they brought Kashyapa's only son aboard, cast off the boat, and tempting him in many ways came to the lord of the Angas."}},{"n":9,"text":"संस्थाप्य तामाश्रमदर्शने तु\nसंतारितां नावमतीव शुभ्राम् ।\nतीरादुपादाय तथैव चक्रे\nराजाश्रमं नाम वनं विचित्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She moored the very bright boat after showing him the hermitage, and the king had the shore taken and made into a wondrous forest called the King's Hermitage."}},{"n":10,"text":"अन्तःपुरे तं तु निवेश्य राजा\nविभाण्डकस्यात्मजमेकपुत्रम् ।\nददर्श देवं सहसा प्रवृष्ट-\nमापूर्यमाणं च जगज्जलेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king lodged Vibhandaka's only son in the women's quarters and suddenly saw the god pouring rain and the world being filled with water."}},{"n":11,"text":"स लोमपादः परिपूर्णकामः\nसुतां ददावृश्यशृङ्गाय शान्ताम् ।\nक्रोधप्रतीकारकरं च चक्रे\nगोभिश्च मार्गेष्वभिकर्षणं च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lomapada, his wishes fulfilled, gave his daughter Shanta to Rishyashringa. He also arranged a defence against the sage's anger, and had cattle driven along the roads."}},{"n":12,"text":"विभाण्डकस्याव्रजतः स राजा\nपशून्प्रभूतान्पशुपांश्च वीरान् ।\nसमादिशत्पुत्रगृद्धी महर्षि-\nर्विभाण्डकः परिपृच्छेद्यदा वः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Vibhandaka was coming, the king ordered many cattle and brave herdsmen: \"If the great sage, eager for his son, asks you,"}},{"n":13,"text":"स वक्तव्यः प्राञ्जलिभिर्भवद्भिः\nपुत्रस्य ते पशवः कर्षणं च ।\nकिं ते प्रियं वै क्रियतां महर्षे\nदासाः स्म सर्वे तव वाचि बद्धाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"you must say with joined hands: 'These cattle and ploughed lands are your son's. Great sage, what pleasing thing shall we do? We are all your slaves, bound to your word.'\""}},{"n":14,"text":"अथोपायात्स मुनिश्चण्डकोपः\nस्वमाश्रमं मूलफलानि गृह्य ।\nअन्वेषमाणश्च न तत्र पुत्रं\nददर्श चुक्रोध ततो भृशं सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the sage of fierce anger came to his hermitage, took roots and fruits, and not finding his son there, he grew very angry."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततः स कोपेन विदीर्यमाण\nआशङ्कमानो नृपतेर्विधानम् ।\nजगाम चम्पां प्रदिधक्षमाण-\nस्तमङ्गराजं विषयं च तस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, tearing with anger and suspecting the king's doing, he went to Champa wishing to burn the lord of the Angas and his country."}},{"n":16,"text":"स वै श्रान्तः क्षुधितः काश्यपस्ता-\nन्घोषान्समासादितवान्समृद्धान् ।\nगोपैश्च तैर्विधिवत्पूज्यमानो\nराजेव तां रात्रिमुवास तत्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tired and hungry, Kashyapa came upon those prosperous cow-settlements, and honoured by the herdsmen as a king would be, stayed the night there."}},{"n":17,"text":"संप्राप्य सत्कारमतीव तेभ्यः\nप्रोवाच कस्य प्रथिताः स्थ सौम्याः ।\nऊचुस्ततस्तेऽभ्युपगम्य सर्वे\nधनं तवेदं विहितं सुतस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Receiving great hospitality from them, he asked, \"Gentle ones, whose are you?\" They all came forward and said, \"This wealth has been provided for your son.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"देशे तु देशे तु स पूज्यमान-\nस्तांश्चैव शृण्वन्मधुरान्प्रलापान् ।\nप्रशान्तभूयिष्ठरजाः प्रहृष्टः\nसमाससादाङ्गपतिं पुरस्थम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honoured in place after place and hearing those sweet words, his anger mostly calmed and he arrived delighted at the lord of the Angas in his city."}},{"n":19,"text":"संपूजितस्तेन नरर्षभेण\nददर्श पुत्रं दिवि देवं यथेन्द्रम् ।\nशान्तां स्नुषां चैव ददर्श तत्र\nसौदामिनीमुच्चरन्तीं यथैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honoured by that best of men, he saw his son in the palace like Indra among the gods, and saw his daughter-in-law Shanta there, like lightning in motion."}},{"n":20,"text":"ग्रामांश्च घोषांश्च सुतं च दृष्ट्वा\nशान्तां च शान्तोऽस्य परः स कोपः ।\nचकार तस्मै परमं प्रसादं\nविभाण्डको भूमिपतेर्नरेन्द्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the villages, the cattle settlements, his son and Shanta, his great anger cooled, and Vibhandaka bestowed great favour on the king."}},{"n":21,"text":"स तत्र निक्षिप्य सुतं महर्षि-\nरुवाच सूर्याग्निसमप्रभावम् ।\nजाते पुत्रे वनमेवाव्रजेथा\nराज्ञः प्रियाण्यस्य सर्वाणि कृत्वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Placing his son there, the great sage said to him, who shone like sun and fire: \"When a son is born, you must return to the forest, having done all that pleases the king.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"स तद्वचः कृतवानृश्यशृङ्गो\nययौ च यत्रास्य पिता बभूव ।\nशान्ता चैनं पर्यचरद्यथाव-\nत्खे रोहिणी सोममिवानुकूला ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rishyashringa did as he said and went to where his father was. Shanta served him properly, devoted as Rohini is to the moon in the sky."}},{"n":23,"text":"अरुन्धती वा सुभगा वसिष्ठं\nलोपामुद्रा वापि यथा ह्यगस्त्यम् ।\nनलस्य वा दमयन्ती यथाभू-\nद्यथा शची वज्रधरस्य चैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As fortunate Arundhati served Vasishtha, as Lopamudra served Agastya, as Damayanti served Nala, as Shachi served the wielder of the thunderbolt,"}},{"n":24,"text":"नाडायनी चेन्द्रसेना यथैव\nवश्या नित्यं मुद्गलस्याजमीढ ।\nतथा शान्ता ऋश्यशृङ्गं वनस्थं\nप्रीत्या युक्ता पर्यचरन्नरेन्द्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"and as Nadayani Indrasena was ever obedient to Mudgala, descendant of Ajamidha, so Shanta, full of love, served Rishyashringa in the forest, king."}},{"n":25,"text":"तस्याश्रमः पुण्य एषो विभाति\nमहाह्रदं शोभयन्पुण्यकीर्तेः ।\nअत्र स्नातः कृतकृत्यो विशुद्ध-\nस्तीर्थान्यन्यान्यनुसंयाहि राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This holy hermitage of that one of holy fame shines here, adorning the great lake. Bathe here, your duty done and purified, king, and then go on to other fords."}}]}]}